ntdll-gamemode-bundle.patch - Gamify patch over CrossOver 25.1.0 Wine (dlls/ntdll/unix), LGPL-2.1-or-later.
macOS Game Mode for Wine programs. macOS turns Game Mode on only for a frontmost, full-screen app
that LaunchServices knows as a game from its bundle's Info.plist; it never reads the Info.plist
linked into the loader (loader-plist-gamemode.patch), so a bare loader never qualified. CW HACK
22144 already runs every child process from a hard link to the loader named after the program,
$TMPDIR/winetemp-<loader id>/<exe>; that link now goes into a minimal bundle,
$TMPDIR/winetemp-<loader id>/<exe>.app/Contents/{Info.plist, MacOS/<exe>} (the loader's plist,
bundle id local.gamify.wine.<exe>, game category, GCSupportsGameMode, LSSupportsGameMode), a hard
link or, across volumes, a copy (a symlink does not work: gamepolicyd follows it and ignores the
process); the flat link stays the fallback. The first process of a launch (no WINESERVERSOCKET,
WINEDLLPATH set) re-execs itself through the same bundle, and an i386 first process goes through
the x87sidecar with the bundled link as its loader (applies on top of loader-rosetta-x87.patch).
Wine's borderless full-screen window counts as full screen; windowed programs stay out of Game Mode.
Details: docs/app.md "Game Mode", NOTES 2026-11-06.

